     2| * IVX technical-debt + freeze-risk scanner.
     3| *
     4| * Walks the workspace source files and surfaces evidence-backed findings the
     5| * autonomous continuous-improvement system can act on:
     6| *   - debt markers   → TODO / FIXME / HACK / TEMP / XXX in real code comments
     7| *   - freeze risks    → empty catch blocks, NOT_IMPLEMENTED / "not implemented"
     8| *                       throws, no-op JSX handlers (onPress/onClick={() => {}})
     9| *   - oversized files → files whose LOC exceeds a maintainability threshold
    10| *
    11| * Every finding carries hard evidence: relativePath + line + snippet + severity
    12| * + a short "why". The marker-scan deliberately targets COMMENT lines (a `//`,
    13| * `/*`, or `*` prefix) so the evidence-gate / detector code that legitimately
    14| * mentions these words as string literals is NOT flagged as debt.
    15| *
    16| * The core (`scanContentForDebt`) is pure and fully unit-testable; the walker
